  "section_notes": "S1 is strong: 24h regulator reporting for all incidents, 24h customer notice, and no phase-in. S2 is weakened because a >5% failure rate triggers review but does not by itself stop sales, though per-model results go to customers and regulators but not the public. S3, S4, and S5 land in acceptable ranges: 6-year retrofit, 36-month suppression, and mandatory 8/100k recall with prompt notice but no serious-injury clause."
